        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat: add disableBoundaryAwareCache compat option for prefix-matching prompt cache providers",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where DeepSeek OpenAI-compatible users could lose provider prompt-cache hits after the 6.x boundary-aware cache split put per-turn dynamic context into the system prompt.\n\nCloses #94518\n\nRelated: #91018, #90583\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nDeepSeek uses prefix-matching cache behavior, so its stable system prefix needs to remain byte-stable across turns. This PR adds `compat.disableBoundaryAwareCache`, defaults it on for DeepSeek, keeps only the stable prefix in the system message, and moves the dynamic suffix into the latest user turn so older conversation history stays reusable. System-only requests preserve that suffix in a trailing runtime-context carrier instead of dropping it.\n\nXiaomi is kept opt-in — users can set `compat.disableBoundaryAwareCache: true` manually, but the automatic default is DeepSeek-only until Xiaomi-specific upstream cache-contract and live-behavior evidence exists.\n\nOperators can opt back into normal boundary-aware behavior with `compat: { disableBoundaryAwareCache: false }`.\n\n## User Impact\n\nDeepSeek users should keep the stable system prompt and prior conversation history cacheable across multi-turn requests without losing dynamic context on system-only requests. Xiaomi users are unaffected by default.\n\n## Evidence\n\nFocused regression tests (rebased on latest `origin/main`):\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs packages/ai/src/providers/openai-completions.test.ts`: 44 passed, including the system-only converter fallback\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/agents/openai-transport-stream.test.ts`: 335 passed, including the system-only DeepSeek payload\n\n### Live DeepSeek cache proof (main vs PR)\n\nEach turn's request is built by the **production** `buildOpenAICompletionsParams`\nand sent to the real DeepSeek API. Native `prompt_cache_hit_tokens` /\n`prompt_cache_miss_tokens` are recorded across 5 repeated turns of one growing\nconversation that **includes a tool loop** (assistant `tool_calls` → `role: tool`).\nEach turn an ephemeral below-boundary context suffix changes (the #94518 driver).\n\n- **Baseline** = `disableBoundaryAwareCache: false`, byte-identical to current\n  `origin/main` `convertMessages` (dynamic suffix stays in `system`).\n- **PR** = DeepSeek auto-on (stable `system` prefix; suffix moved to latest user).\n\n```text\n                  BASELINE (== current main)        PR (this change)\nturn 1 (cold):    hit=0     miss=2373               hit=0     miss=2373\nturn 2:           hit=0     miss=2408               hit=2304  miss=104\nturn 3:           hit=1920  miss=523                hit=2304  miss=139\nturn 4:           hit=1920  miss=558                hit=2304  miss=174\nturn 5:           hit=1920  miss=593                hit=2304  miss=209\n\nwarm turns 2..5:  hit=5760  miss=4082               hit=9216  miss=626\n```\n\nReading: on `main` the mutating `system` suffix caps cache at the stable\ninstruction block (`hit` plateaus at 1920) and the growing history + tool result\n**never** cache, so `miss` climbs each turn. With the PR the instruction block\nplus accumulated history/tool-result stay cacheable (`hit` plateau 2304, `miss`\nonly the new turn). Across warm turns the PR yields **+60% cache-hit tokens** and\n**~85% fewer billed miss tokens** — the cost regression #94518 reports. Values\nreproduced across two runs; API key redacted.\n\nAI-assisted: built with Codex\n",
        "branch": "fix/deepseek-boundary-aware-cache-94518",
